Serve this repo as the plain static files it is, with no Jekyll build.

GitHub Pages runs Jekyll by default, and Jekyll renders every .md in the repo
as Liquid — including docs/superpowers/plans/*.md, which quote test fixtures.
One of those fixtures contains a bare `{{`, and Liquid treats it as the start
of a variable it never finds the end of:

  Rendering Liquid: docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-12-panel-mission-cards.md
  Error: Liquid syntax error (line 657): Variable '{{', stderr: 'lease boom',
  timedOut: false }' was not properly terminated with regexp: /\}\}/

That broke every deploy from 2026-08-14 (when the file merged) to 2026-08-24,
silently: the build fails, Pages keeps serving the last good commit, and the
site looks fine while being ten days stale. Two PRs' worth of work never
reached production.

Nothing here needs Jekyll — no _config.yml, no Gemfile, no layouts, just
index.html and its scripts. This file also stops Jekyll from hiding anything
whose name starts with an underscore.
